// N64 role-split exact BF16 gate+up+SwiGLU fusion for gfx1151.
// Waves 0-3 own gate and waves 4-7 own up, retaining one plane's
// accepted accumulator chain per wave and the native two-tier cadence.
// High-capacity two-tier streamed MXFP4 expert-stationary MUL_MAT_ID for gfx1151.
//
// Each workgroup owns 128 output rows of one expert. Experts with at most 16
// matches use one accumulator; larger routed cohorts use the paired
// two-window loop. Four adjacent canonical K32 records remain register-resident
// while their BF16 RHS fragments are exchanged within each wave.
// host_cache begins with int32 slot_map[1024] followed by the immutable
// begin-layer residency cohort map. The global slot ID dynamically selects
// device_cache for slots [0, D) or host_cache for slots [D, D + H). No expert
// identity or tier is compiled into the kernel.

